      "problem": "Max needs to solve all of the exercises in $\\frac{3}{2}$ pages of a math book. If he has already solved $\\frac{2}{5}$ of the exercises, how many pages of exercises has Max solved?",
      "worked_solution": "To find out the number of pages Max solved, we need to calculate $\\frac{2}{5}\\times \\frac{3}{2}.$\n\nTo multiply the two numbers, we multiply the numerators, and we multiply the denominators:\n\n$$\n\\frac{2}{5}\\times \\frac{3}{2}=\\frac{2\\times 3}{5\\times 2}=\\frac{6}{10}\n$$\n\nNext, we simplify:\n\n$$\n\\frac{6}{10}=\\frac{6÷2}{10÷2}=\\frac{3}{5}\n$$\n\nSo, Max solved $\\frac{3}{5}$ pages.",
